ovides a significant boost for them as well on the game of 24. We see that both Claude 3 and Gemini 1.5","level":1,"path_id":"1~38","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":37,"section_id":"sec-1~38"},{"title":"Table 7 .","text":"7Performance comparison of AoT with traditional dynamic programming methods on solving Coin Change and Edit Distance problems.Pro benefit significantly. We were unable to run Gemini 1.5 Pro on CoT-SC due to API access not being available yet. Please refer to Table8for detailed results.Method GPT-4 Claude 3 Gemini 1.5 ProIO7%6%6%CoT-SC9%9%-AoT71%68%55%","level":1,"path_id":"1~39","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":38,"section_id":"sec-1~39"},{"title":"Table 9 .","text":"9Performance of the methods determined by GPT-4.MethodScore Avg. QueriesStandard Prompting 6.191CoT6.931ToT7.5620AoT7.581\n\t\t\tDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Virginia Tech, Blacksburg, USA. Correspondence to: Bilgehan Sel &lt;bsel@vt.edu&gt;.","level":1,"path_id":"1~40","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":39,"section_id":"sec-1~40"}],"citations":[{"raw_text":"Decision-focused learning for inverse noncooperative games: Generalization bounds and convergence analysis\n\t\t\n\t\t\tAAl-Tawaha\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tHKaushik\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tBSel\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tRJia\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tJin\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tM\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tIFAC-PapersOnLine\n\t\t\n\t\t\t56\n\t\t\t2\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t2023","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"Decision-focused learning for inverse noncooperative games: Generalization bounds and convergence analysis","anchors":[{"ref_id":"b0","section_path_id":"1.","quote":"Al-Tawaha et al., 2023;","offset":4288}]},{"raw_text":"A singular value thresholding algorithm for order estimation\n\t\t\n\t\t\tASAl-Tawaha\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tKAljanaideh\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tAAlshorman\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\t2021 American Control Conference (ACC)\n\t\t\n\t\t\tIEEE\n\t\t\t2021","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"A singular value thresholding al